                <pb facs="0186" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg20"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.6521/100</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Italian Ambassador
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: Referring to Mr.
                    Brambilla’s recent call at the Department, relative to the conflict of the
                    so-called Seamen’s Act, approved March 4, 1915, with certain treaty provisions
                    between this Government and Italy, I beg to transmit, herewith, for your
                    information, a copy of an instruction dated March 23, regarding the matter,
                    which has been sent to the American Ambassador at Rome.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
